<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tlaxcalans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tlaxcalan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tlaxcalans were the people of Tlaxcala, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> confederation east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> that remained independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>. They were long-standing enemies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> and fought repeated ritual wars with them. When the Spanish arrived in 1519 the Tlaxcalans became their most important allies, providing thousands of warriors for the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>.</p></div>
